    {
      "id": "be8f26e6-b572-4e5f-a851-15d6fa82f3e4",
      "phaseId": "09bcb3cf-f8ea-454a-913e-ea377c53d37e",
      "number": 83,
      "shortId": "SJDWB",
      "priority": 1,
      "shortName": "wasm-host-api",
      "title": "Design WASM host API facade",
      "status": "planned",
      "description": "API host esposta ai plugin WASM.\n\n═══ SETTLE THIS BEFORE DESIGNING THE FACADE (cross-reference added 2026-07-25) ═══\nFull write-up: F003/P017/T9 (deferred there on purpose — this is where it gets decided).\n\nFor a plugin author to get ANY editor completion, the builder types must live somewhere their crate\ncan depend on. Today they cannot:\n- The declarative model — `ViewNode`, `WidgetKind`, `PropValue`, `Intent` — lives INSIDE THE APP at\n  heca/src/chrome/view.rs. A plugin is a separate program and cannot depend on the app.\n- The workspace has six members and none is a plugin kit: heca-core, heca-renderer, heca-config,\n  heca-grid-ui, heca, heca-theme (Cargo.toml:2). docs/chrome-and-ui.md never names one\n  either.\n- F003/P011/T006 (typed builder SDK) says \"the WASM SDK re-exports it\". With the model in the app\n  crate, that sentence cannot currently be true of anything.\n\nThis IS the phase that has to answer it, because the host API facade is exactly the boundary in\nquestion. Do not design the facade around types a plugin cannot import.\n\nNOT the forbidden thing: AGENTS.md:744 rejects `heca-grid-ui` owning `ViewNode` (it inverts the\ncrate graph, and `ViewNode` cannot carry the closures/signals native chrome needs). A separate small\ncrate ALONGSIDE, depended on by both the app and plugins, inverts nothing — a different question,\nand the user's to decide. Do not treat the settled rule as having already answered it, and do not\ntreat this note as permission.\n\nAlso in scope for the same decision: a plugin written in JavaScript or Python gets no Rust\ncompletion regardless. The widget vocabulary is a CLOSED list with a coverage guard already walking\nit (`WidgetKind::ALL`), so matching definitions for other languages could be generated from it —\nuncosted. Check whether F003/P017/T3's generated property tables are reusable for that rather than\nprivate to the app.",
      "notes": "",
